# Docker build context is the repo root (`context: ..` in
# deploy/docker-compose.yml). Everything listed here is excluded from
# what's sent to the daemon and from what `COPY . .` in deploy/Dockerfile
# copies into the image.

# Host-installed deps: `RUN npm ci` in the Dockerfile already installs a
# fresh, Linux-native node_modules inside the image. If the host's
# node_modules were copied in afterward by `COPY . .`, it would overwrite
# native binaries (e.g. Prisma's query engine) with Windows-incompatible
# ones, and would also bloat the build context by ~900MB and defeat layer
# caching.
node_modules

# Rebuilt fresh by `npm run build` inside the image.
.next

# Never needed at build or run time.
.git

# Runtime data directories — bind/volume-mounted by docker-compose.yml,
# never baked into the image.
var
backups

# Secrets are injected via docker-compose's `environment:` block, never
# baked into the image. Also blocks deploy/.env.dryrun used for local
# dry-runs.
.env
.env.*

# Local-only artifacts.
*.log
coverage
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.claude
